<main class="listing-page content-width">
  <div class="page-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span>{" "}ABOUT THE AUTHOR</span>
    <h1>Jeffrey <em>Caballero.</em></h1>
    <p>Batch 2011. The alumnus who keeps this wall standing.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="about-layout">
    <figure class="author-photo" tabindex="0">
      <div class="author-photo-frame">
        <div class="author-photo-layer author-photo-now"><img src="/author-now.jpg" alt="Now" /></div>
        <div class="author-photo-layer author-photo-before"><img src="/author-then.jpg" alt="Batch 2011" /></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Jeffrey Caballero · Developer · Author</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>
        The Freedom Wall was ours. As far as I remember it belonged to our years
        and no other — a thing of our time at Baleno, where we said what we could
        not say out loud: confessions, jokes, dedications, small heartbreaks
        pinned up for the whole school to read. Time takes the paper down. This
        site is my attempt to keep that wall standing, so the notes from our
        years are still there when we come looking for them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Balik Baleno is also meant to be somewhere to belong. After graduation we
        scatter across cities and countries, and the group chats go quiet for
        years at a time. Here you can find your batch again, leave a note on the
        wall, or just read and remember the school on the hill that shaped us.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is a personal project: independent, unofficial, and kept small on
        purpose. I built it as an alumnus of Batch 2011, for everyone who ever
        walked those corridors.
      </p>

